---
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, REPO_URL, SENDER } from "../../shared/site";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "27 October 2026";
const mail = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`;
---

<Base title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using the headmesh.dev website and waitlist." ogImage="terms">
  <article class="container-page pt-16 sm:pt-24">
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        These terms cover your use of the headmesh.dev website, its documentation and the waitlist, run by
        {SENDER.legalName} ("we"). By using the site you agree to them.
      </p>

      <h2>The waitlist</h2>
      <p>
        Joining the waitlist is free. It doesn't guarantee access to Headmesh or to any particular feature, and we may
        send invitations in any order. You can leave at any time with the unsubscribe link in our emails.
      </p>

      <h2>The software</h2>
      <p>
        Headmesh's source code is published in its <a href={REPO_URL}>GitHub repository</a> and is licensed under the
        terms stated there, not these. Headmesh is pre-release software: features described on this site may change or
        not ship.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>Please don't:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>sign up anyone other than yourself;</li>
        <li>try to get around the spam protection, overload the site or probe it for vulnerabilities outside our
          <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security policy</a>;</li>
        <li>use the site to break the law or infringe anyone's rights.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Names and trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        "Headmesh" and the Headmesh logo identify our project. Tailscale, Headscale, WireGuard and other names belong
        to their owners and are used here only to describe compatibility. Headmesh isn't affiliated with or endorsed by
        them. WireGuard is a registered trademark of Jason A. Donenfeld.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The site and everything on it are provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, to the extent the law
        allows. Documentation describes software under active development and may be incomplete or out of date.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, we aren't liable for indirect or consequential losses arising from your use of
        the site. Nothing in these terms limits liability that can't be limited by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href={mail}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
